<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 10px; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 5th Grade (CEFR: A1.3)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Taking Care of Our Class</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Let's Arrange the Chairs.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Text: Explain simple written instructions to peers. Communication: Facilitate discussions on classroom topics among peers.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can explain written instructions with simple steps and gestures (e.g., "Please, wipe down the desks." and mimics wiping down the desks). Can facilitate discussions by asking classmates questions, encouraging answers, and using gestures like nodding to prompt responses (e.g., "How can you help keep the classroom clean?"). Can summarize classroom responsibilities for peers, using basic words and gestures (e.g., "We put away our supplies." and points to a labeled supply bin).</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of key concepts and language for mediation.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up: "Classroom Chore Charades"</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows flashcards of classroom objects (chair, desk, whiteboard, trash can, mop, dustpan).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher mimes a cleaning action (e.g., sweeping, wiping, arranging) and students guess the action using target verbs: "Are you sweeping?", "Are you wiping?".</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students use "Yes, I am." or "No, I'm not. I'm arranging." Teacher encourages full sentences and pronunciation of /r/ in "arrange" and /s/ in "supply".</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling: Explaining Instructions with Gestures</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher picks up a small piece of trash and a trash can. Teacher says, "Please, put away the trash," and mimes the action.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher then points to a messy area of chairs and says, "Let's arrange the chairs quickly," demonstrating arranging them while saying "quickly".</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher demonstrates using polite language and gestures when giving instructions. "Can you help me wipe the table?" (gestures wiping).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'Sweep the floor,' do I clean the window or the floor?" (Floor!)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'Please arrange the chairs,' what should you do with the chairs?" (Put them in order!)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Taking Care of Our Class".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> "Classroom Cleaning Steps" Poster (a simple, illustrated poster with 3-4 steps for keeping the classroom tidy).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Examples of instructions on the poster:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. Sweep the floor. (Picture of sweeping)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. Wipe the desks. (Picture of wiping)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. Arrange the chairs. (Picture of arranging)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">4. Put away the supplies. (Picture of putting away)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Explain simple written instructions to peers, using basic words and gestures.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher shows the poster. Students identify the pictures and match them to the written instructions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher reads each instruction aloud. Students repeat chorally, focusing on pronunciation of /r/ and compound words like "whiteboard" (white-board, two syllables).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher asks: "What is step number one?" "What are we doing in picture number three?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation skills for explaining and facilitating discussions.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Explaining instructions, offering help, facilitating discussions. Grammar: Imperatives (e.g., "Sweep."), Present Continuous (e.g., "We are sweeping."), Modal "can" (e.g., "Can I help you sweep?"). Vocabulary: chair, desk, sweep, wipe, arrange, organize, put away, clean up, supplies.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1: Instruction Match-up.</b> Students receive cards with cleaning actions (e.g., "Sweep the floor," "Wipe the whiteboard") and picture cards. In pairs, they match the written instruction to the correct picture. Then, they take turns explaining one instruction to their partner using gestures. E.g., Student A shows "Sweep the floor" card and mimes sweeping, saying, "Please, sweep the floor."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2: "What are we doing?" Sentence Completion.</b> Teacher displays images of people cleaning (e.g., someone wiping a window, someone arranging chairs). Students complete sentences using the present continuous. E.g., "They are ______ the window." (wiping). Or use "can" to offer help: "______ you help me ______ the chairs?" (Can, arrange).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3: Peer Instruction Chain.</b> In small groups, students are given a sequence of 2-3 simple written instructions (e.g., "1. Wipe the table. 2. Put away the bucket."). Student A explains the first instruction to Student B using "please" and gestures. Student B confirms understanding. Then Student B explains the second instruction to Student C. This fosters politeness and understanding. Teacher monitors for use of "please" and correct pronunciation.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Taking Care of Our Class".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task: "Explain Our Cleaning Instruction Poster" (21st Century Skills Project)</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students, in their project groups, present their "Cleaning Instruction Poster" (designed in previous lessons) to another group or the whole class.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group member takes turns explaining at least one illustrated instruction from their poster to their peers. They must use imperatives (e.g., "Let's sweep the floor."), polite language ("Please, wipe down the desks."), and clear gestures to support their explanation.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After explaining their instructions, each group facilitates a brief discussion with their audience by asking questions about classroom cleanliness (e.g., "How can you help keep the classroom clean?"), nodding to encourage answers, and summarizing key responsibilities. (e.g., "So, we put away our supplies and arrange the chairs.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher monitors for fluency, use of target language, politeness, and effective mediation.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy and student self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy: Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Feedback</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher uses a checklist to observe each student's ability to explain instructions, use gestures, and facilitate discussion during the poster presentation.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Audience groups provide brief, constructive peer feedback using "two stars and a wish" (two things they liked, one suggestion).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Groups explain 2-3 instructions from their Cleaning Instruction Poster to another group. They must include: an imperative, the word "please", a gesture, and one question to engage the audience. Each group also summarizes their poster's message using basic words. Example: "We are cleaning our class, please wipe the desks." "How can you help?" "We clean up!"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and intelligibility of explanation.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (nouns, verbs, adverbs).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of imperatives and the modal "can".</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Consistent use of "please" and supportive gestures.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to ask a question and facilitate peer interaction.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaboration and clear division of roles within the group.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I explain the instructions clearly to my classmates? Yes / No"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did I use 'please' and gestures when I explained? Yes / No"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one way I can help keep our classroom clean?" (Students write or draw.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Student and teacher reflection on the lesson's effectiveness.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of explaining instructions was easy for me?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part was difficult, and how can I practice it more?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this mediation lesson? Were students actively explaining and facilitating?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students successfully integrate the target grammar (imperatives, present continuous, 'can'), vocabulary, and pragmatic functions (politeness)?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for students to better explain and discuss in English? (e.g., more sentence frames, specific practice for asking questions).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson concludes the "Taking Care of Our Class" theme. The next lesson will introduce a new theme, possibly expanding on classroom rules or community responsibilities, building on the collaborative and polite language practiced here.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>